# Minimal subtext (admin + product UI)

Applies to `apps/web/**` and UI pattern docs (e.g. `apps/web/DESIGN.md`).

## Principle

Minimize subtexts, helper paragraphs, subtitles under headings, and redundant explanatory copy. The interface should read from primary elements: labels where needed, icons, visual state, and `aria-label` / `sr-only` for accessibility.

## Prefer

- Self-explanatory controls (checkbox + icon, color-coded slots, drag handles)
- Tooltips (`title`) for optional detail — not visible flankerende tellers
- Error/recovery copy only when action fails (`role="alert"`)
- `sr-only` or `aria-label` instead of visible helper lines

## Subtext only when

- Legal / compliance disclosure
- Destructive action confirmation
- Non-obvious error recovery (user cannot infer next step from UI alone)
- Accessibility requires visible text beyond `aria-label` (rare; prefer visible primary label over a separate hint)

## Reference: Category Health (`/admin/categories/health`)

Raster-first layout — no counters or labels flanking the slot grid:

- **Filter:** checkbox + filter icon, `aria-label="Alleen actie nodig"` — no visible caption or hint below
- **Legend:** icon swatches + `sr-only` labels — no inline text labels beside swatches
- **Rows:** drag handle + category names + slot grid — no “sleep rijen…” helper paragraph
- **Empty state:** icon + short headline — no explanatory paragraph

When adding admin dashboards or dense data views, follow this pattern before adding helper copy.
